Core changes needed to run under WebAssembly.

- jsiConsolePrintf/jsjcDebugPrintf: pass a callback with the vcbprintf_callback signature
  instead of casting jsiConsolePrint. WebAssembly traps on calls through a function pointer
  of the wrong type (it is undefined behaviour in C, harmless on ARM/x86).
- jsiIdle: like EMSCRIPTEN, sleep (return to the host) even though USB is "connected".
- jshTransmit: send console output through the transmit buffer (for the host to read)
  rather than to stdout as on LINUX.
- jsvAddressToVar: Storage is memory-mapped on WASM, so return a flash-backed string
  instead of copying the file into RAM (which fails for large .bootcde files).
- poke8/16/32: map the address with jshFlashGetMemMapAddress, as peek already does, so
  the WASM target can give device addresses (registers, CCM RAM) somewhere to live.
- E.nativeCall: throw instead of jumping into ARM machine code.
- jsuGetFreeStack (LINUX): ESPR_STACK_SIZE overrides the assumed 1 MB stack, so an emulator
  can match a device's stack (it decides, for example, whether Storage can be compacted).

